## Findings (settled — positive and negative; append-only, never trimmed)

The campaign's accumulated knowledge. An entry lands here only after multiple consistent experiments
AND a CONFIRMED verdict from `{{VERIFY_SKILL}}`'s independent refuter — **every entry cites its
`results/verdicts/<id>.json` by name; a claim with no verdict citation is an open thread, not a
finding, and steers nothing.** A single good run is a Recent-experiments line, not a finding.
Steering-negatives are findings too (number them N1, N2, …): record the **kill tier** from the
verdict — REFUTED (mechanism understood → prunes) or EVIDENCE AGAINST (clean single negative →
shelved in `results/queue.json`, revivable; entries accumulate toward a prune). An INCONCLUSIVE kill
never lands here; queue a fix-and-rerun unit. Narrative depth stays in the logbook — one to three
lines per entry, citing exp ids.

Disputes and retractions are appended, never resolved by deletion: challenge an entry with a dated
**DISPUTES Fn** line (what is contested, on what evidence); overturn or narrow one with a dated
**REVISES Fn** entry and edit Fn's first line to begin `[SUPERSEDED — see REVISES below]`, keeping
its original text, then amend the stale claim wherever it was copied (scoreboard `notes`,
`../../../PROJECT_ORIENTATION.md`). A finding that is a fact about the **system** — not a config
that scored well — is additionally promoted to the project ledger `../../../DISCOVERIES.md`, citing
the same verdict artifact (that write is hook-gated).

- F1 · <the settled claim, one line> · exp <ids> · `verdicts/<id>.json` · <mechanism/scope, one line>

